  [1m5. Call sites[0m

  [38;5;153mapp.js[39m — all four [38;5;153mconsole.*[39m calls convert. The password variable is never passed to a logging call; it goes to [38;5;153mlogin()
[39m  and nowhere else. [38;5;153mconsole.error("Validation error:", …)[39m becomes [38;5;153mlog.warn(…)[39m, since a user leaving a field blank is
  not an application error.

  [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m — one judgment call: [38;5;153mconsole.log(greet('world'))[39m is the program's [1moutput[0m, not a diagnostic. I'd leave it
  as [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m and add a separate [38;5;153mlog.debug("startup")[39m. Routing stdout output through a logger is how CLIs end up
  unpipeable.

  [1m6. Testing and tooling[0m

  The repo has no runner, no linter, no formatter, and no dependencies. Cheapest moment to fix that is now. My
  recommendation is [1munit tests only[0m, using Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m — zero dependencies, matching the repo's current
  posture — with [38;5;153m"test": "node --test"[39m in package.json. Coverage: level filtering, redaction of nested and array-nested
  keys, depth cap, sink dispatch order, and that both export paths yield a working logger.

  I'd skip linting/formatting for now (eslint+prettier is the first [38;5;153mnode_modules[39m in this repo, a real change in
  character) and skip e2e entirely — there's no server and one form.

